  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">2024 GRANT-ENHANCE ROLE OF CBVS IN COMMUNITY BASED</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The First 1000 Most Critical Days Programme proposed the creation of a network of Nutrition Support Groups (NSGs) to improve the coverage and convergence of priority nutrition interventions at household level. The NSG model in Zambia has succeeded in improving reach and multi-sectoral convergence across the 17 districts. With this once-off grant, UNICEF will promote a community health system strengthening approach that adapts and mainstreams the NSG model into existing MoH structures to ensure their sustainability, especially against the backdrop of shrinking donor support to nutrition.</narrative>
  </description>
